		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A concise body cannot START with `@`, so a DECORATED class expression at the body's",
			"start": 20,
			"end": 106
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " leftmost position takes a paren pair of its own — around the class alone, exactly as",
			"start": 108,
			"end": 195
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " a leftmost object literal does. The pair breaks open, since the decorator owns a line.",
			"start": 197,
			"end": 286
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A decorated class DIVIDED keeps the shape. There the pair is the dividend's own — the",
			"start": 508,
			"end": 596
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " one every function or class expression left of `/` takes — so it is printed once.",
			"start": 598,
			"end": 682
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A frozen body whose ROOT is the class takes the same pair — it is the position's, so",
			"start": 737,
			"end": 824
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " it rides outside the slice.",
			"start": 826,
			"end": 856
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " prettier-ignore",
			"start": 878,
			"end": 896
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A frozen COMPOSITE body — one whose leftmost node is the class rather than the body's",
			"start": 920,
			"end": 1008
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " root — carries that pair INSIDE the slice: acorn's member and call spans begin at the",
			"start": 1010,
			"end": 1098
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " author's `(`, so the freeze takes the pair along with the class and prints it back",
			"start": 1100,
			"end": 1185
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " verbatim. The position-pair seam the expression statement also uses is what mints the",
